# Local tooling state — background subagents (e.g. issue implementers spawned from planning
# sessions) work in isolated git worktrees under .claude/worktrees/, not repo content. Local,
# machine-specific settings aren't repo content either. .claude/skills/ (and anything else under
# .claude/) IS repo content and should be tracked — e.g. the pm-workflow skill.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
